<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bias of Priene</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bias of Priene was a Greek statesman of the 6th century BCE, counted among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-sages-of-greece">Seven Sages of Greece</a>. Known for his judgement in legal disputes, he advised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionians">Ionians</a>, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, to sail together to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and found a single city there rather than live under Persian rule. Sayings such as 'most men are bad' were attributed to him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bias-of-priene.jpg" alt="Bias of Priene" width="320" height="538" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bias_Pio-Clementino_Inv279.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
